# What never reaches a build context.
#
# Every image in this repository builds from the repository ROOT, because each
# one spans workspaces: core-api compiles against gen/go and libs/chassis, web
# installs through the Bun workspace at the root, intelligence copies
# gen/python. So there is one context for all of them and one ignore file
# governing it, and an entry here has to be safe for every image rather than
# only for the one being added.
#
# The entries are not tidiness. The daemon transfers the whole context before
# the first instruction runs, so an unignored directory is time and memory
# spent on every build of every service.
#
# THE ONE THAT MATTERS MOST IS deploy/models. It holds the GGUF weights the
# model service serves, which is 2.7 GB for the default pin and more for a
# larger one. It lives on the host rather than in a named volume so that
# `down -v` does not cost a re-download (see compose), and that same choice
# puts it inside the build context, where it would otherwise be uploaded to
# the daemon before every single build.

.git
.github

# Agent worktrees. `.claude/worktrees/` holds a full checkout per branch in
# flight, so on a machine doing parallel work this one line is the difference
# between a context of tens of megabytes and one of several gigabytes.
.claude

# Installed trees. Every image installs its own dependencies from a manifest
# and a lockfile, which is the point of committing the lockfile: copying a
# host's node_modules would ship whatever that host resolved, for whatever
# platform it runs, on top of the resolution the image just performed.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__

# Build output. web's image runs `next build` itself, so a `.next` from a host
# build is at best redundant and at worst a stale mix of two builds.
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
test-results
playwright-report

# Model weights. See the note above: gigabytes, and no image needs them.
deploy/models

# Local configuration and secrets. `.env.local` is written by
# scripts/web-env.sh from a running stack and holds the OAuth client secret
# Zitadel generated; it has no business in an image layer.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
*.swp

# Nothing here changes an image, and a change to one of them should not
# invalidate a cached layer.
*.md
!apps/intelligence/README.md
docs
postman
scratch
